IMPORT `mc15-nouns`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: THE PREAMBLE AND CHAPTER 1.
-- The preamble (the King's style and greeting, the reasons for the grant, the enacting
-- words and the names of those who advised) creates no rule; it is listed in NOTES.md as
-- inert, reason 1, and is not quoted here.  Chapter 1 grants the English church her
-- freedom and every freeman the liberties of the Charter.
-- Terms the text does not define and this module takes as plain facts: "freeman".
-- GENERATED from tools/templates/mc15-ch01.l4.in by tools/build.py; edit the template.

§ `Preamble and chapter 1`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- the English church shall be free`

-- src:9 | In the first place we have granted to God, and by this our present charter confirmed for us and our heirs for ever that the English church shall be free, and shall have her rights entire, and her liberties inviolate;
-- src:9 | and we will that it be thus observed;
@ref Chapter 1 clause 1.1-1.2 (src:9)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 1 -- the English church shall be free, with her rights entire and her liberties inviolate` IS
    PARTY `the King`
    SHANT `infringe the freedom of the English church, her rights or her liberties`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 1: the freedom, rights or liberties of the English church were infringed"

-- src:9 | and this we will observe, and our will is that it be observed in good faith by our heirs for ever.
@ref Chapter 1 clause 1.4 (src:9)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 1 -- the freedom of elections of the English church shall be observed` IS
    PARTY `the King`
    SHANT `interfere with the freedom of elections of the English church`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 1: the freedom of elections of the English church was interfered with"

§§ `Chapter 1 -- the liberties granted to freemen`

-- gloss (not the text's): "freeman" is asked as a plain fact, and so is being the heir of one.
-- src:9 | We have also granted to all freemen of our kingdom, for us and our heirs forever, all the underwritten liberties, to be had and held by them and their heirs, of us and our heirs forever.
@ref Chapter 1 clause 1.5 (src:9)
GIVEN `the person is a freeman of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the heir of a freeman of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` IS
    IF   `the person is a freeman of the kingdom`
      OR `the person is the heir of a freeman of the kingdom`
    THEN Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`
